" (https://www.belfuse.com/media/datasheets/products/power-supplies/ds-bps-pfe1100-12-054xa.pdf)\nciteturn8view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 5 days ago; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 25; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.belfuse.com/media/datasheets/products/power-supplies/ds-bps-pfe1100-12-054xa.pdf\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 1150\nL0@P0: The PFE1100-12-054xA is a 1100 Watt AC to DC power-factor\u0002corrected (PFC) power supply that converts standard AC mains power\nL1@P0: into a main output of 12 VDC for powering intermediate bus\nL2@P0: architectures (IBA) in high performance and reliability servers, routers,\nL3@P0: and network switches.\nL4@P0: The PFE1100-12-054xA meets international safety standards and\nL5@P0: displays the CE-Mark for the European Low Voltage Directive (LVD).\nL6@P0: • Best-in-class, 80 PLUS certified “Platinum” efficiency\nL7@P0: • Wide input voltage range: 90-264 VAC\nL8@P0: • AC input with power factor correction\nL9@P0: • Always-On 16.5 W programmable standby output (3.3/5 V)\nL10@P0: • Hot-plug capable\nL11@P0: • Parallel operation with active digital current sharing\nL12@P0: • Full digital controls for improved performance\nL13@P0: • High density design: 25.6 W/in3\nL14@P0: • Small form factor: 321.5 x 54.5 x 40 mm (12.66 x 2.14 x 1.57 in)\nL15@P0: • I\nL16@P0: 2C communication interface for control, programming and\nL17@P0: • monitoring with PSMI and Power Management Bus protocol\nL18@P0: • Overtemperature, output overvoltage and overcurrent protection\nL19@P0: • 256 Bytes of EEPROM for user information\nL20@P0: • 2 Status LEDs: AC OK and DC OK with fault signaling\nL21@P0: • High Performance Servers\nL22@P0: • Routers\nL23@P0: • Switches\nL24@P0-1: Please read our datasheet & drawing disclaimer here.2 PFE1100-12-054xA\nL25@P1: tech.support@psbel.com\nL26@P1: PFE 1100 - 12 - 054 x A\nL27@P1: Product Family Power Level Dash V1 Output Dash Width Airflow Input\nL28@P1: PFE Front-Ends 1100 W 12 V 54 mm N: Normal\nL29@P1: R: Reverse A: AC\nL30@P1: The PFE1100-12-054xA AC/DC power supply is a fully DSP controlled, highly efficient front-end power supply. It incorporates\nL31@P1: resonance-soft-switching technology and interleaved power trains to reduce component stresses, providing increased system\nL32@P1: reliability and very high efficiency. With a wide input operational voltage range and minimal linear derating of output power with input\nL33@P1: voltage and temperature, the PFE1100-12-054xA maximizes power availability in demanding server, network, and other high\nL34@P1: availability applications. The supply is fan cooled and ideally suited for integration with a matching airflow paths.\nL35@P1: The PFC stage is digitally controlled using a state-of-the-art digital signal processing algorithm to guarantee best efficiency and unity\nL36@P1: power factor over a wide operating range. The DC/DC stage uses soft switching resonant techniques in conjunction with synchronous\nL37@P1: rectification. An active OR-ing device on the output ensures no reverse load current and renders the supply ideally suited for operation\nL38@P1: in redundant power systems. The always-on standby output, with selectable voltage level (3.3/5.0 Volts), provides power to external\nL39@P1: power distribution and management controllers. It is protected with an active OR-ing device for maximum reliability.\nL40@P1: Status information is provided with front-panel LEDs. In addition, the power supply can be controlled and the fan speed set via the\nL41@P1: I\nL42@P1: 2C bus. The I2C bus allows full monitoring of the supply, including input and output voltage, current, power, and inside temperatures.\nL43@P1: Cooling is managed by a fan controlled by the DSP controller. The fan speed is adjusted automatically depending on the actual power\nL44@P1: demand and supply temperature and can be overridden through the I2C bus.\nL45@P1: Figure 1. PFE1100-12-054xA Block Diagram\nL46@P1: Stresses in excess of the absolute maximum ratings may cause performance degradation, adversely affect long-term reliability and\nL47@P1: cause permanent damage to the supply.\nL48@P1: PARAMETER CONDITIONS / DESCRIPTION MIN MAX UNITS\nL49@P1: Vi maxc Maximum Input Continuous 264 VAC\nL50@P1: Logic Signals\nL51@P1: V1Sense+\nL52@P1: L Buck\nL53@P1: Aux Converter\nL54@P1: VsbSense+ VsbSense\u0002GND\nL55@P1: V1\nL56@P1: Vsb N PFC DC\nL57@P1: DC\nL58@P1: Digital Prim Controls V1Sense- I2C PWM Filter\nL59@P1: PE PWM\nL60@P1: Communication Bus APS Digital Sec Controls\nL61@P1-2: EEPROM FANPFE1100-12-054xA 3\nL62@P2: Asia-Pacific\nL63@P2: +86 755 298 85888\nL64@P2: Europe, Middle East\nL65@P2: +353 61 49 8941\nL66@P2: North America\nL67@P2: +1 866 513 2839\nL68@P2: © 2023 Bel Fuse Inc. BCD.00012_AP\nL69@P2: General Condition: TA = 0… 45 °C unless otherwise noted.\nL70@P2: PARAMETER DESCRIPTION / CONDITION MIN NOM MAX UNITS\nL71@P2: Vi nom Nominal Input Voltage 100 230 230 VAC\nL72@P2: Vi Input Voltage Ranges Normal operating (Vi min to Vi max) 90 264 VAC\nL73@P2: Vi red Derated Input Voltage Range See Figure 20 and Figure 40 90 180 VAC\nL74@P2: Ii max Max Input Current 13 Arms\nL75@P2: Ii p Inrush Current Limitation Vi min to Vi max, TNTC = 25°C (\nL76@P2: Figure 5)\nL77@P2: 40 Ap\nL78@P2: Fi Input Frequency 47 50/60 64 Hz\nL79@P2: PF Power Factor Vi nom, 50Hz, > 0.3 I1 nom 0.96 W/VA\nL80@P2: Vi on Turn-on Input Voltage1 Ramping up 80 87 VAC\nL81@P2: Vi off Turn-off Input Voltage1 Ramping down 75 85 VAC\nL82@P2: η Efficiency without Fan\nL83@P2: Vi nom, 0.1∙Ix nom, Vx nom, TA = 25°C 90.3\nL84@P2: %\nL85@P2: Vi nom, 0.2∙Ix nom, Vx nom, TA = 25°C 93.4\nL86@P2: Vi nom, 0.5∙Ix nom, Vx nom, TA = 25°C 94.5\nL87@P2: Vi nom, Ix nom, Vx nom, TA = 25°C 93.8\nL88@P2: Thold Hold-up Time After last AC zero point, V1 > 10.8V, VSB within\nL89@P2: regulation, Vi = 230 VAC, Px nom\nL90@P2: 12 ms\nL91@P2: 1 The Front-End is provided with a minimum hysteresis of 3 V during turn-on and turn-off within the ranges.\nL92@P2: INPUT FUSE\nL93@P2: Quick-acting 16 A input fuses (5 x 20 mm) in series with both the L- and N-line inside the power supply protect against severe\nL94@P2: defects. The fuses are not accessible from the outside and are therefore not serviceable parts.\nL95@P2: INRUSH CURRENT\nL96@P2: The AC-DC power supply exhibits an X-capacitance of only 3.2 μF, resulting in a low and short peak current, when the supply\nL97@P2: is connected to the mains. The internal bulk capacitor will be charged through an NTC which will limit the inrush current.\nL98@P2: NOTE:\nL99@P2: Do not repeat plug-in / out operations within a short time, or else the internal in-rush current limiting device (NTC) may not\nL100@P2: sufficiently cool down and excessive inrush current or component failure(s) may result.\nL101@P2: INPUT UNDER-VOLTAGE\nL102@P2: If the sinusoidal input voltage stays below the input undervoltage lockout threshold Vi on, the supply will be inhibited. Once the\nL103@P2: input voltage returns within the normal operating range, the supply will return to normal operation again.\nL104@P2: POWER FACTOR CORRECTION\nL105@P2: Power factor correction (PFC) is achieved by controlling the input current waveform synchronously with the input voltage. A\nL106@P2: fully digital controller is implemented giving outstanding PFC results over a wide input voltage and load ranges. The input current\nL107@P2: will follow the shape of the input voltage. If for instance the input voltage has a trapezoidal waveform, then the current will also\nL108@P2: show a trapezoidal waveform.\nL109@P2: In addition, the PFC circuit has a stability region to be observed when operating the power supply at high input current\nL110@P2: amplitudes. At a low source inductance (<150 μH) the power supply will work stable up to its full maximum input current (13\nL111@P2: Arms). If the source inductance is higher, the region with stable PFC operation is slightly reduced (as shown in Figure 4). The\nL112@P2-3: power supply will also work in the unstable region, but it may exhibit a slight current oscillation during the sinusoidal peak.4 PFE1100-12-054xA\nL113@P3: tech.support@psbel.com\nL114@P3: EFFICIENCY\nL115@P3: High efficiency (see Figure 2) is achieved by using state-of-the-art silicon power devices in conjunction with soft-transition\nL116@P3: topologies minimizing switching losses and a full digital control scheme. Synchronous rectifiers on the output reduce the losses\nL117@P3: in the high current output path. The speed of the fan is digitally controlled to keep all components at an optimal operating\nL118@P3: temperature regardless of the ambient temperature and load conditions.\nL119@P3: Figure 2. Efficiency vs. Load current (ratio metric loading) Figure 3. Power factor vs. Load current\nL120@P3: Figure 4. PFC Stability Region Figure 5. Inrush current, Vin = 230Vac, 90°\nL121@P3: CH4: Vin (200V/div), CH3: Iin (20A/div)\nL122@P3: 88\nL123@P3: 89\nL124@P3: 90\nL125@P3: 91\nL126@P3: 92\nL127@P3: 93\nL128@P3: 94\nL129@P3: 95\nL130@P3: 0 200 400 600 800 1000\nL131@P3: Po [W]\nL132@P3: Efficiency [%]\nL133@P3: Vi = 230Vac, fan internal\nL134@P3: Vi = 230Vac, fan external\nL135@P3: Platinum\nL136@P3: 0.8\nL137@P3: 0.82\nL138@P3: 0.84\nL139@P3: 0.86\nL140@P3: 0.88\nL141@P3: 0.9\nL142@P3: 0.92\nL143@P3: 0.94\nL144@P3: 0.96\nL145@P3: 0.98\nL146@P3: 1\nL147@P3: 0 200 400 600 800 1000\nL148@P3: Po [W]\nL149@P3: Power factor\nL150@P3: Vi = 230Vac\nL151@P3: Vi = 115Vac\nL152@P3: 0\nL153@P3: 2\nL154@P3: 4\nL155@P3: 6\nL156@P3: 8\nL157@P3: 10\nL158@P3: 12\nL159@P3: 14\nL160@P3: 16\nL161@P3: 0 100 200 300 400 500 600 700 800 900 1000\nL162@P3: Line Inductance [uH]\nL163@P3: Input Current [Arms]\nL164@P3: Stable\nL165@P3-4: UnstablePFE1100-12-054xA 5\nL166@P4: Asia-Pacific\nL167@P4: +86 755 298 85888\nL168@P4: Europe, Middle East\nL169@P4: +353 61 49 8941\nL170@P4: North America\nL171@P4: +1 866 513 2839\nL172@P4: © 2023 Bel Fuse Inc. BCD.00012_AP\nL173@P4: General Condition: Ta = 0 … +45