P5: External capacitor V1 dV1max Unit\nL253@P5: 2Pcs 47 µF/16 V/X5R/1210 150 mVpp\nL254@P5: 1Pcs 1000 µF/16 V/Low ESR\nL255@P5: Aluminum/ø10x20 120 mVpp\nL256@P5: 1Pcs 270 µF/16 V/Conductive\nL257@P5: Polymer/ø8x12 120 mVpp\nL258@P5: 2Pcs 47 µF/16 V/X5R/1210 plus\nL259@P5: 1Pcs 270 µF Conductive Polymer\nL260@P5: OR 1Pcs 1000 µF Low ESR AlCap\nL261@P5: 60 mVpp\nL262@P5: Table 1. Suitable capacitors for V1\nL263@P5: External capacitor VSB dV1max Unit\nL264@P5: 1Pcs 10 µF/16 V/X5R/1206 80 mVpp\nL265@P5: 2Pcs 10 µ/F16 V/X5R/1206 50 mVpp\nL266@P5: 1Pcs 47 µF/16 V/X5R/1210 40 mVpp\nL267@P5: 2Pcs 100 µF/6.3 V/X5R/1206 30 mVpp\nL268@P5: Table 2. Suitable capacitors for VSB\nL269@P5: The output ripple voltage on VSB is influenced by the main output V1. Evaluating VSB output ripple must be done when\nL270@P5: maximum load is applied to V1.\nL271@P5: Figure 7. Turn-On AC Line 230VAC, full load (200ms/div)\nL272@P5: CH1: V1 (2V/div) CH2: VSB (2V/div) CH3: Vin (200V/div)\nL273@P5: Figure 8. Turn-On AC Line 230VAC, full load (5ms/div)\nL274@P5: CH1: V1 (2V/div) CH2: VSB (2V/div) CH3: Vin (200V/div)\nL275@P5: V1\nL276@P5: PGND\nL277@P5: VSB PFExxxx-12-054NA\nL278@P5-6: Connection boardPFE1100-12-054xA 7\nL279@P6: Asia-Pacific\nL280@P6: +86 755 298 85888\nL281@P6: Europe, Middle East\nL282@P6: +353 61 49 8941\nL283@P6: North America\nL284@P6: +1 866 513 2839\nL285@P6: © 2023 Bel Fuse Inc. BCD.00012_AP\nL286@P6: Figure 9. Turn-Off AC Line 230VAC, full load (20ms/div)\nL287@P6: CH1: V1 (2V/div) CH2: VSB (2V/div) CH3: Vin (200V/div)\nL288@P6: Figure 10. Short circuit on V1 (500 μs/Div)\nL289@P6: CH1: V1 (2V/div) CH2: VSB (1V/div) CH3: I1 (200A/div)\nL290@P6: Figure 11. Short circuit on V1 (50ms/div)\nL291@P6: CH1: V1 (2V/div) CH2: VSB (1V/div) CH3: I1 (200A/div)\nL292@P6: Figure 12. AC drop out 10 ms (10ms/div)\nL293@P6: CH1: V1 (2V/div) CH2: VSB (1V/div) CH4: Vin (200V/div)\nL294@P6: Figure 13. AC drop out 20 ms (10ms/div)\nL295@P6: CH1: V1 (5V/div) CH2: VSB (2V/div) CH4: Vin (200V/div)\nL296@P6: Figure 14. AC drop out 20ms (200ms/div), V1 restart after 1s\nL297@P6: CH1: V1 (5V/div) CH2: VSB (2V/div) CH4: I1 (200V/div)\nL298@P6: Figure 15. Load transient V1, 5 to 50A (500μs/div)\nL299@P6: CH2: V1 (200mV/div), CH4: I1 (20A/div)\nL300@P6: Figure 16. Load transient V1, 50 to 5A (500μs/div)\nL301@P6-7: CH2: V1 (200mV/div), CH4: I1 (20A/div)8 PFE1100-12-054xA\nL302@P7: tech.support@psbel.com\nL303@P7: Figure 17. Load transient V1, 40 to 85A (500μs/div)\nL304@P7: CH2: V1 (200mV/div), CH4: I1 (20A/div)\nL305@P7: Figure 18. Load transient V1, 85 to 40A (500μs/div)\nL306@P7: CH2: V1 (200mV/div), CH4: I1 (20A/div)\nL307@P7: PARAMETER DESCRIPTION / CONDITION MIN NOM MAX UNIT\nL308@P7: F Input Fuses (L+N) Not user accessible, quick-acting (F) 16 A\nL309@P7: V1 OV OV Threshold V1 13.3 14.5 VDC\nL310@P7: tOV V1 OV Latch Off Time V1 1 ms\nL311@P7: VSB OV OV Threshold VSB 115 125 % VSB\nL312@P7: tOV VSB\nL313@P7: OV Latch Off Time\nL314@P7: VSB\nL315@P7: 1 ms\nL316@P7: IV1 lim\nL317@P7: Current Limit V1\nL318@P7: PFE1100-12-054NA\nL319@P7: Vi > 115VAC, Ta < 45°C\nL320@P7: Vi > 90VAC, Ta < 45°C\nL321@P7: 93.5\nL322@P7: 74\nL323@P7: 100\nL324@P7: 78 A\nL325@P7: Current Limit V1\nL326@P7: PFE1100-12-054RA\nL327@P7: Vi > 180VAC, Ta < 45°C\nL328@P7: Vi > 90VAC, Ta < 45°C\nL329@P7: 92\nL330@P7: 72\nL331@P7: 100\nL332@P7: 78\nL333@P7: IV1 SC\nL334@P7: Max Short Circuit\nL335@P7: Current V1\nL336@P7: V1 < 3V 110 A\nL337@P7: tV1 SC\nL338@P7: Short Circuit\nL339@P7: Regulation Time V1 < 3V, time until IV1 is limited to < IV1 sc 2 ms\nL340@P7: tV1 SC off\nL341@P7: Short Circuit Latch\nL342@P7: Off Time Time to latch off when in short circuit 200 ms\nL343@P7: TSD\nL344@P7: Over Temperature on\nL345@P7: Heat Sinks Automatic shut-down 115 °C\nL346@P7: 6.1 OVERVOLTAGE PROTECTION\nL347@P7: The PFE front-ends provide a fixed threshold overvoltage (OV) protection implemented with a HW comparator. Once an OV\nL348@P7: condition has been triggered, the supply will shut down and latch the fault condition. The latch can be unlocked by\nL349@P7: disconnecting the supply from the AC mains or by toggling the PSON_L input.\nL350@P7: 6.2 VSB UNDERVOLTAGE DETECTION\nL351@P7: Both main and standby outputs are monitored. LED and PWOK_H pin signal if the output voltage exceeds ±5% of its nominal\nL352@P7: voltage. Output undervoltage protection is provided on the standby output only. When VSB falls below 75% of its nominal\nL353@P7: voltage, the main output V1 is inhibited.\nL354@P7: 6.3 CURRENT LIMITATION\nL355@P7: MAIN OUTPUT\nL356@P7: The main output exhibits a substantially rectangular output characteristic controlled by a software feedback loop. If it runs in\nL357@P7: current limitation and its voltage drops below ~10.0 VDC for more than 200 ms, the output will latch off (standby remains on).\nL358@P7-8: 6PFE1100-12-054xA 9\nL359@P8: Asia-Pacific\nL360@P8: +86 755 298 85888\nL361@P8: Europe, Middle East\nL362@P8: +353 61 49 8941\nL363@P8: North America\nL364@P8: +1 866 513 2839\nL365@P8: © 2023 Bel Fuse Inc. BCD.00012_AP\nL366@P8:  Figure 19. Current Limitation on V1 (Vi = 230 VAC)\nL367@P8: A second current limitation circuit on V1 will immediately switch off the main output if the output current increases beyond the\nL368@P8: peak current trip point. The supply will re-start 4 ms later with a soft start, if the short circuit persists (V1 < 10.0V for >200 ms)\nL369@P8: the output will latch off; otherwise it continuous to operate (hardware current limit triggers).\nL370@P8: The latch can be unlocked by disconnecting the supply from the AC mains or by toggling the PSON_L input.\nL371@P8: The main output current limitation will decrease if the ambient (inlet) temperature increases beyond 45°C or if the AC input\nL372@P8: voltage is too low (see Figure 20 and Figure 21). Note that the actual current limitation on V1 will begin at a current level\nL373@P8: approximately 4 A higher than what is shown in Figure 20. (See also Temperature and Fan Control for additional information.)\nL374@P8: STANDBY OUTPUT\nL375@P8: The standby output exhibits a substantially rectangular output characteristic down to 0V (no hiccup mode / latch off). If it runs\nL376@P8: in current limitation and its output voltage drops below the UV threshold, then the main output will be inhibited (standby remains\nL377@P8: on). The current limitation of the standby output is independent of the AC input voltage, but is derated with the ambient\nL378@P8: temperature (only for reverse airflow).\nL379@P8: Figure 20. Derating on V1 vs. Vi and Ta for\nL380@P8: PFE1100-12-054NA\nL381@P8: Figure 21. Derating on V1 vs. Vi and Ta for\nL382@P8: PFE1100-12-054RA\nL383@P8: Figure 22. Current limitation on VSB Figure 23. Temperature derating on VSB\nL384@P8: 0\nL385@P8: 2\nL386@P8: 4\nL387@P8: 6\nL388@P8: 8\nL389@P8: 10\nL390@P8: 12\nL391@P8: 0 20 40 60 80 100\nL392@P8: Main Output Current [A]\nL393@P8: Main Output Voltage [V]\nL394@P8: 0\nL395@P8: 20\nL396@P8: 40\nL397@P8: 60\nL398@P8: 80\nL399@P8: 100\nL400@P8: 90 115 140 165 190 215 240 265\nL401@P8: Input AC Voltage [VAC]\nL402@P8: Main Output Nominal Current [A]\nL403@P8: Ta < 35°C\nL404@P8: Ta < 45°C\nL405@P8: Ta < 55°C\nL406@P8: Ta < 65°C\nL407@P8: 0\nL408@P8: 20\nL409@P8: 40\nL410@P8: 60\nL411@P8: 80\nL412@P8: 100\nL413@P8: 90 115 140 165 190 215 240 265\nL414@P8: Input AC Voltage [VAC]\nL415@P8: Main Output Nominal Current [A]\nL416@P8: Ta < 35°C\nL417@P8: Ta < 45°C\nL418@P8: Ta < 55°C\n"
